m the award in 2013 and his story \\\"Genesis\\\" was shortlisted for the 2016 Caine Prize. Folarin's first novel, A Particular Kind of Black Man, was released ... \",\"title\":\"https://guides.loc.gov/african-jewish-middle-east-studies/african-studies/event-videos\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Life Apart (2010), which won the Writers' Guild of Great Britain Award for Best Fiction Book; The Lives of Others (2014), which was shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize and the Costa Best Novel Award, and won the Royal Society of Literature's Encore Award; and A ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... White Tiger | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2009 | Hilary Mantel | Wolf Hall | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2010 | Howard Jacobson | The Finkler Question | Comic novel | |\\n| 2011 | Julian Barnes | The Sense of an Ending | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2012 | Hilary Mantel | Bring Up the Bodies | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2013 | Eleanor Catton | The Luminaries | Historical fiction | |\\n| 2014 | Richard Flanagan .\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1935\\n\\nThe is a Japanese literary award presented biannually. Because of its prestige and the considerable attention the winner receives from the media, it is, along with the Naoki Prize, one of Japan's most sought after literary prizes.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nThe Akutagawa Prize was established in 1935 by ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ak