ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2007\\n*Yōko Ogawa, 2007\\n*Masahiko Shimada, 2010\\n*Hikaru Okuizumi, 2012\\n*Shuichi Yoshida, 2016\\n*Hisaki Matsuura, 2019\\n*Keiichiro Hirano, 2020\\n*Mieko Kawakami, 2024\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* List of Japanese literary awards\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nCategory:1935 establishments in Japan\\nCategory:Awards established in 1935\\nCategory:Japanese-language literary awards\\nCategory:Japanese literary ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akutagawa_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ukrainian Poetry Series—which features translations of preeminent Ukrainian poets, presented in dual-language format.\\n\\nShortly after its founding, Holbert moved Lost Horse Press to Sandpoint, Idaho, and in 2004 she established the Idaho Prize for Poetry, a national poetry competition awarding prize money and publication to a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.clmp.org/programs-opportunities/firecracker/firecracker-awards-winners-archive/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was also awarded France's Prix Femina for a work in translation. Her seventh novel, Someone, was a New York Times bestseller, a finalist for the Dublin IMPAC Award, the National Book Critics Circle Award, the Patterson Prize for Fiction, and the Dayton Literary Peace Prize. Three ... \",\"title\":\"https://missionandministry.georgetown.edu/conference-participants/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... His work has been translated into over 12 languages. He founded and edits the acclaimed literary journal, Conjunctions, which is celebrating its fortieth anniversary this year, the last three decades of which have been published by Bard College. As well as editing some 75 book-length issues of ... \",\"title\":\"https://literature.bard.edu/faculty/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... Asian fiction, and was a finalist for both the Man Booker prize and the National Book Award in fiction.\\n\\nLahiri's first book written in Italian, In Altre Parole, later published in English as In Other Words, explores the often emotionally fraught links between identity and language. Her ... \",\"title\":\"https://carolinaperformingarts.org/events/jaipur-literature-festival-usa/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... He serves on the advisory boards of the Man Asian Literary Prize, the Indo-US Commission on Museums and Culture, the German Research Foundation, and the Graduate School of North American Studies and the International Research Center \\\"Interweaving Performance Cultures\\\" at Free University Berlin. He has received honorary ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.infosysprize.org/about-the-prize/categories/humanities.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was longlisted for the Man Asian Literary Prize in 2011. However, after the 2012 anti-Japanese demonstrations in China, Murakami's books were removed from sale there, along with those of other Japanese authors. Murakami criticized the China–Japan political territorial dispute, characterizing the overwrought nationalistic ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruki_Murakami\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6a1b02f33bef61b0daa3a08f272e777ef9de7a4e0a9b6d1d2d6a76efe384aa59\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"13f63279ce8fee7c9391f65b354671eb0f3f9e60721e66a91a51c224e1b61d8d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize established 2007 translated 25 languages\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_66e39214b22643a6bbe4b85d"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure. The award was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" Let me think about the Jan Michalski Prize (created 2009) and other awards. Let me search for the Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia page directly.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Jan Michalski Prize winners list 2010s\", \"Jan Michalski Prize for Literature founded 2009\", \"Jan Michalski Prize shortlist translated 25 languages\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_c5bde356fb014eaebe3c6ebc","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2002-12-17\\n---\\nThis is a partial list of notable Polish or Polish-speaking or -writing people. People of partial Polish heritage have their respective ancestries credited.\\n\\nPhysics\\n\\n*Miedziak Antal\\n* Czesław Białobrzeski\\n* Andrzej Buras\\n* Georges Charpak, 1995 Nobel Prize\\n* Jan Kazimi